# Failure dynamics over time (channel signature): one server under overload. Generic, ILLUSTRATIVE; no clock times. Sources: AWS Builders' Library, Google SRE book ch. 21-22.
...@_style
grid-rows: 7
grid-columns: 2
grid-gap: 12
h0: "stage" {class: note}
h1: "what happens (generic server, illustrative)" {class: note}
a0: "1 · first event" {class: bad}
a1: "traffic climbs, or capacity drops\n(surge, lost fleet, cheap-to-expensive requests)" {class: svc}
b0: "2 · signal" {class: warn}
b1: "latency crosses the client's timeout:\nthroughput stays high, goodput collapses" {class: svc}
c0: "3 · shared resource" {class: bad}
c1: "threads and queues fill;\nretries multiply the offered load" {class: svc}
d0: "4 · containment" {class: ok}
d1: "shed by priority, newest first,\nwithin an adaptive limit, as early as you can" {class: ok}
e0: "5 · trade-off" {class: ext}
e1: "some requests are refused on purpose;\noverall availability drifts down" {class: ext}
f0: "6 · recovery" {class: ok}
f1: "goodput holds, then load ramps back gradually" {class: ok}
